#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:142
msgid ""
"Place a root option before the command path. Name the exact profile on "
"the target command when it accepts a profile target. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:149
msgid ""
"This source is used only after the exact profile is known, the command "
"requires a profile session, no matching live session exists, and "
"persisted-session resume has failed. It is refused without being read "
"when the command does not need profile authentication, when the exact "
"target already has a live or resumed session, or when the command is "
"self-authenticating. Login, create, restore, logout, and passphrase "
"change do not accept this root proof."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:156
msgid ""
"On a host without usable keychain persistence, successful root "
"authentication continues only the current process. The command emits a "
"Notice that the passphrase must be supplied again in the next process. "
"Each new process repeats the Argon2 password derivation; this deliberate "
"cost is not cached in a weaker credential or transferable bearer token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:162
msgid "Keep two secret sources distinct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:164
msgid "Choose sources before either is read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:166
msgid "Do not select both stdin and a descriptor for the same option pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:167
msgid "Do not assign stdin to both the root and leaf scopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:168
msgid "Do not assign the same descriptor number to both scopes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:169
msgid ""
"Use root fd plus leaf stdin, root stdin plus leaf fd, or two different "
"descriptors when one invocation needs both objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:172
msgid ""
"A selected source that does not apply to the resolved command or exact "
"profile is refused as unused. This protects scripts from sending a "
"credential to the wrong target after a command-line mistake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:176
msgid "Pass an inherited descriptor safely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:178
msgid ""
"Use an anonymous pipe when standard input already carries another value. "
"The caller owns the descriptor's backing object and lifetime. Cadrumo "
"performs one bounded read and closes the descriptor locally after reading"
" begins, including on refusal. Descriptor `0` is allowed as a stdin-"
"equivalent; descriptors `1` and `2`, negative descriptors, closed "
"descriptors, and unreadable descriptors are refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:185
msgid ""
"On POSIX, start the process with the pipe's read descriptor in the child "
"process's `pass_fds` allowlist, then pass that number to `--secrets-fd` "
"or `--profile-secrets-fd`. On Windows, do not assume a numeric CRT "
"descriptor is inherited directly. Allowlist an inheritable Windows HANDLE"
" and use the supported bootstrap wrapper to convert it with "
"`msvcrt.open_osfhandle`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:195
msgid ""
"Omit `--profile-handle` or `--secrets-handle` when the invocation needs "
"only one scope. The wrapper inserts the matching canonical descriptor "
"option; do not also add it to the command tail. Prefer the stdin channel "
"for a directly launched portable command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:200
msgid ""
"Cadrumo bounds the input, wipes mutable read buffers on a best-effort "
"basis, and releases secret-bearing references promptly. Python may create"
" immutable strings while decoding JSON and validating secret fields, so "
"the application does not claim guaranteed memory erasure. Never reuse the"
" pipe, redirect it to a regular file, or log the JSON object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:206
msgid ""
"Interactive commands may prompt only on a verified terminal. A redirected"
" or non-interactive invocation without the required explicit channel is "
"refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:209
msgid "Log out of the active profile"
msgstr "Kijelentkezés az aktív profilból"

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:211
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Run `aeat config logout` when you finish working with a profile. Logout "
"closes the active storage session, discards in-memory key material, "
"disposes the bucket engines, and keeps the profile selected for the next "
"exact login:"
msgstr ""
"Futtassa az `aeat config logout` parancsot, amikor befejezi a munkát egy "
"profillal. A kijelentkezés lezárja az aktív tárolási munkamenetet, "
"eldobja a memóriában lévő kulcsanyagot, megszünteti a bucket-motorokat, "
"és törli az aktív-profil kiválasztást:"

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:219
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Nothing in the profile is deleted. Log in again with `aeat config login` "
"to use the selected profile, or name another exact profile when you "
"return."
msgstr ""
"A profilban semmi nem törlődik. Jelentkezzen be újra az `aeat config "
"login <name>` paranccsal, amikor visszatér."

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:222
msgid "Reset local state (last resort)"
msgstr "A helyi állapot visszaállítása (végső eset)"

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:224
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Export every profile you want to keep before continuing. Reset "
"permanently deletes every profile stored locally, related local "
"authentication state, and the active profile selection. It doesn't delete"
" exports stored elsewhere. You can't undo the reset. Deleting is also not"
" a way to hide activity: any copies of your data that left the machine "
"(exports, filings, backups) are outside Cadrumo's control and nothing in "
"Cadrumo can retract them."
msgstr ""
"Exportáljon minden megtartani kívánt profilt, mielőtt folytatná. A "
"visszaállítás véglegesen töröl minden helyben tárolt profilt, a "
"kapcsolódó helyi hitelesítési állapotot és az aktív-profil kiválasztást. "
"Nem törli a máshol tárolt exportokat. A visszaállítás nem vonható vissza."

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:234
msgid ""
"Use `start` only when you intend to remove all local profiles. Confirm "
"the reset explicitly. It checks retention requirements before deleting "
"anything and refuses to start while another reset is incomplete."
msgstr ""
"A `start` értéket csak akkor használja, amikor minden helyi profilt el "
"akar távolítani. Erősítse meg a visszaállítást kifejezetten. A törlés "
"előtt ellenőrzi a megőrzési követelményeket, és megtagadja az indítást, "
"amíg egy másik visszaállítás befejezetlen."

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:237
msgid ""
"Use the read-only `status` command to inspect the latest operation "
"without changing local data. Provide an operation ID to inspect an exact "
"operation. Status reports an incomplete, paused, or complete operation. "
"Its output includes the operation ID and any pause reason."
msgstr ""
"Használja a csak olvasható `status` parancsot a legutóbbi művelet "
"megvizsgálásához a helyi adatok módosítása nélkül. Adjon meg egy "
"műveletazonosítót egy pontos művelet megvizsgálásához. A státusz egy "
"befejezetlen, szüneteltetett vagy befejezett műveletet jelent. Kimenete "
"tartalmazza a műveletazonosítót és bármely szünet okát."

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:241
msgid ""
"Use `resume` after an interruption or pause. Confirm the reset again. It "
"continues the same incomplete operation instead of creating another. "
"Provide an operation ID to resume an exact operation. After deletion "
"starts, resuming the reset doesn't restore deleted data."
msgstr ""
"Használja a `resume` parancsot egy megszakítás vagy szünet után. Erősítse"
" meg újra a visszaállítást. Ugyanazt a befejezetlen műveletet folytatja, "
"ahelyett hogy egy másikat hozna létre. Adjon meg egy műveletazonosítót "
"egy pontos művelet folytatásához. A törlés megkezdése után a "
"visszaállítás folytatása nem állítja vissza a törölt adatokat."

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:246
msgid ""
"If legal retention requirements pause the reset, stop if you must keep "
"the affected records. Override the pause only after reviewing and "
"accepting the legal retention consequence, and always provide a non-empty"
" reason. If you provide a reason without the override, the command "
"refuses to continue."
msgstr ""
"Ha jogi megőrzési követelmények szüneteltetik a visszaállítást, álljon "
"meg, ha meg kell tartania az érintett rekordokat. Csak a jogi megőrzési "
"következmény felülvizsgálata és elfogadása után írja felül a szünetet, és"
" mindig adjon meg egy nem üres indokot. Ha felülírás nélkül ad meg "
"indokot, a parancs megtagadja a folytatást."

